---
code: transport-apply-failed
when-fires: a remote apply ran to completion and its artifact exited non-zero. cli/main.rs ship_consented_apply. {host} is the destination, {status} the status the completion marker carried.
why: law-lane-discipline. The third world state in the transport family and the only KNOWN one: it ran, it finished, it exited non-zero. The status is reproduced, never interpreted. A zero is equally not a health claim - plans/252 section 8 - which is what a verify re-probe is for.
---
-- webhost.dorc-plan.sh --
#!/bin/sh
false

-- edge-fault --
transport apply-failed 2

-- replay --
$ export DORC_SEED=0

$ dorc apply --host web1.example.net --plan webhost.dorc-plan.sh
apply: error[transport-apply-failed]: The apply artifact on web1.example.net ran
to completion and exited 2; the status is the artifact's own, and a fresh `dorc
plan` measures what actually converged.
apply: recorded intent c02e48a7f9cff5ed0ff9086402e75e03f2b9446a573d1a03d93e95cf523a5f80 and outcome 74341e7fb3d150a2b3454043a7207aa6c68e7661d3485f411dd450cb32e36e59 -- dorc why takes either id

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: transport-apply-failed
{{host}} = "web1.example.net"
{{status}} = "2"
{{v0}} = "c02e48a7f9cff5ed0ff9086402e75e03f2b9446a573d1a03d93e95cf523a5f80"
{{v1}} = "74341e7fb3d150a2b3454043a7207aa6c68e7661d3485f411dd450cb32e36e59"
